{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793372058,"nonce":"m9KhgmfF9OzcznNFUh/hx7C3PN4=","title":"Present a streamed surface in Ashui: texture upload, scaling, input capture and focus","message":"A preview-tab component that draws the current frame scaled to the tab (fit, integer scaling, device pixel ratio), replaces pixels per frame without allocating a Bitmap each time, and captures raw pointer (buttons, wheel, touch), keyboard (repeat, layouts, IME composition), focus, pointer capture and resize, and forwards them as protocol input. Needs an updatable RGBA texture in Ashui (asked of ashui: a CanvasFrame paint hook with writeTexture, or a media Player); canvas-kit is editor-shaped and not the surface. Keyboard focus must not leak shortcuts to the workbench while the app has focus, and must leave it by an explicit gesture. Reuse AppPreview's chrome, bounds binding, overlay handling and release-on-close. Check cost per 1280x720 frame in the WASM page against the heap limits (ashui 54e0e0e).\n\nPart of the framework previews epic: git-bug 9c6f60e27c2cb4be92d534eccc95910e303a5c4e03e1e8779c6d52ca9c40a330","files":null}]}